Operation Operator Method Description Union <code>A | B</code> <code>A.union(B)</code> Elements present in either A, B, or both Intersection <code>A &amp; B</code> <code>A.intersection(B)</code> Elements present in BOTH A and B Difference <code>A - B</code> <code>A.difference(B)</code> Elements in A that are NOT in B Symmetric Diff <code>A ^ B</code> <code>A.symmetric_difference(B)</code> Elements in either A or B, but NOT both Example: Set Operations <pre><code>set_a = {1, 2, 3, 4}
set_b = {3, 4, 5, 6}

print("Union (|):             ", set_a | set_b)
print("Intersection (&amp;):      ", set_a &amp; set_b)
print("Difference (A - B):    ", set_a - set_b)
print("Symmetric Difference (^):", set_a ^ set_b)
</code></pre> Output  Union (|):              {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6} Intersection (&amp;):       {3, 4} Difference (A - B):     {1, 2} Symmetric Difference (^): {1, 2, 5, 6}

ListsDictionariesSets <pre><code>lst = [1, 2, 3]
lst.append(4)          # [1, 2, 3, 4]
lst.extend([5, 6])     # [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]
